  "material_learning": "Armed-to-signal latency is causal, decision-time available, selective and broad across all five annual folds, but late confirmations are not low-value DRA entries. The 168-hour veto reduced Validation realized and total PnL by 16.54059476 USDT, slightly increased drawdown by 0.193109 percentage points, increased maximum underwater duration by 34 hours and extended P90 holding by 1191.9 hours. Every annual total-PnL delta was negative, and both rejection-only neighbors also reduced Validation realized and total PnL. Waiting longer inside the parent armed window is not an adverse-quality factor for this strategy.",
